            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0791" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg777"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish, Secretary of State, to Mr. Hoar,
                        Attorney-General.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 8,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[40]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Roberts,
                    the minister of Spain, late in the business hours, yesterday, orally represented
                    to this Department that he had <pb facs="0792" n="778" xml:id="pg778"/>
                    information to the effect that the steamer Quaker City was being fitted out and
                    armed at New York for the purpose of cruising against Spanish commerce under a
                    letter of marque. I at once telegraphed to General Barlow, the marshal, to
                    inquire into the matter, with a view to further proceedings. It is, however,
                    suggested that you give him such further official instructions as you may deem
                    advisable.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>HAMILTON FISH.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. R. Hoar</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
